 To apply a Gaussian filter before the Sobel edge detection algorithm in MATLAB, you need to add a few lines of code to your existing script. Here's how you can do it:
```
% Read input image
input_image = imread('image.jpg');
% Convert to grayscale
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);
% Apply Gaussian filter
gaussian_filter = fspecial('gaussian', [3 3], 0.5); % Set standard deviation as desired (e.g., 0.5)
smoothed_image = imfilter(gray_image, gaussian_filter);
% Define Sobel operators in x and y directions
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];
% Apply Sobel operator in x direction
edge_image_x = conv2(double(smoothed_image), sobel_x, 'same');
% Apply Sobel operator in y direction
edge_image_y = conv2(double(smoothed_image), sobel_y, 'same');
% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
% Display edge image
imshow(edge_image);
```
This modified code applies a Gaussian filter using the `fspecial()` function before smoothing the image with the Sobel operator. The standard deviation of the Gaussian filter can be adjusted by changing the second argument in the `fspecial()` function call.

